.TITLE "tracert"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Determines the path taken to a destination by sending ICMP Echo Request messages with varying Time to Live (TTL) values. It identifies each __hop__ in the network path.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**tracert hostname**
Traces the path to the specified hostname or IP address.
> __hostname__ the target destination

**tracert -d hostname**
Prevents tracert from resolving IP addresses to hostnames for faster results.
> __-d__ no-resolution flag

**tracert -h 20 hostname**
Specifies the maximum number of hops to search for the target.
> __-h 20__ max hops flag

**tracert -w 500 hostname**
Sets the timeout in milliseconds to wait for each reply.
> __-w 500__ timeout flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __tracert__ helps identify where a network connection is failing or which router is causing latency. It provides a detailed view of the internet infrastructure between you and the host.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**windows:ping** **windows:netstat**

documentation: __https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/tracert__
